@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+# CI triage: build 1219, test (3.12)
+
+- `clock.utc_now()` (used by `expiry_after()` when no start is given, i.e. by the new `Inventory.extend()`) called `datetime.utcnow()`, which is deprecated in Python 3.12; our pytest config turns warnings into errors, so both extend tests failed. It also returned a naive datetime from the wall clock instead of the inventory's injected clock.
+- `discounts.parse_expiry()` returned naive datetimes for offset-less strings and dates, so `Discount.is_active()` compared them with the aware UTC `now` and raised "can't compare offset-naive and offset-aware datetimes".
+- Fix: `utc_now()` returns `datetime.now(UTC)`, `extend()` computes the new expiry from `self._clock.now()`, and `parse_expiry()` returns aware UTC (offset-less values are UTC, offsets are converted), so the library never mixes naive and aware datetimes and does not depend on the local time zone.
